# Copy to .env.local and adjust.
#
# Server-side only. The browser never sees any of this: every API call goes
# through the same-origin proxy at /api/backend, which attaches the bearer
# token. There are deliberately no NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables -- the browser has
# no reason to know where the API lives.

# Required. No fallback: a missing value fails the request that needs it with
# a message naming this variable, rather than silently pointing nowhere.
LMS_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1

# Optional. How long the API has to *start* responding, in milliseconds
# (default 30000). This bounds time-to-first-byte only -- a large CSV export
# or file download streams for as long as it needs once its headers arrive.
# Without a bound, an unresponsive API leaves the console on a spinner
# indefinitely rather than showing an error.
# LMS_API_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# Optional. The header a reverse proxy in front of this server sets to the
# browser's IP address, e.g. x-real-ip for nginx's
# `proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;`. The API records that address in
# the audit trail. Set it ONLY when that proxy is the sole way to reach this
# server (production binds the port to 127.0.0.1); otherwise a browser could
# send the header itself and choose the address it is recorded under. Unset
# (local development), client addresses are recorded as unknown.
# LMS_CLIENT_IP_HEADER=x-real-ip
